+    <main class="page-container"><a href="/HermeticDB/texts.html" class="back-link">← Return to Library</a><h1 class="title-large">CH XIII: On Rebirth</h1><div class="card-meta" style="margin-bottom:3rem">PRIMARY_SOURCE</div><div class="prose-content"><p>CH XIII is a secret discourse on the mountain where Hermes instructs Tat in the mystery of rebirth (<i><i>Palingenesia</i></i>). It is a highly ritualized dialogue where Hermes reveals that the 'Self' is born of God's will and that the physical body is a prison of the twelve 'punishments' (vices) which must be driven out by the ten 'powers' (virtues).</p><div class="themes-container" style="margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border)"><span style="color:var(--text-muted); font-size:0.9rem; margin-right:1rem">KEY THEMES:</span><a href="/HermeticDB/concepts/theurgy.html" class="theme-tag">Theurgy</a> <a href="/HermeticDB/concepts/regeneration.html" class="theme-tag">Regeneration</a> <a href="/HermeticDB/concepts/palingenesia.html" class="theme-tag">Palingenesia</a> <a href="/HermeticDB/concepts/deification.html" class="theme-tag">Deification</a></div></div></main>
