-    <main class="page-container"><a href="/HermeticDB/texts.html" class="back-link">← Return to Library</a><h1 class="title-large">Theatrum Chemicum Britannicum</h1><div class="card-meta" style="margin-bottom:3rem">PRIMARY_SOURCE</div><div class="prose-content"><p>The <i>Theatrum Chemicum Britannicum</i> (1652) is Elias Ashmole's monumental compilation.</p><h2>Scholarly Significance</h2><p>Ashmole preserved the indigenous English alchemical tradition by publishing obscure verse manuscripts from figures like Thomas Norton and George Ripley, preventing the destruction of this heritage during the English Civil War.</p></div></main>
