-    <main class="page-container"><a href="/HermeticDB/dictionary.html" class="back-link">← Return to Dictionary</a><h1 class="title-large"><p>Prisca Theologia</p></h1><div class="card-meta" style="margin-bottom:3rem">THEOLOGICAL Concept · ACTOR TERM</div><div class="prose-content"><p>The <i>Prisca Theologia</i> (Ancient Theology) is a historiographical concept developed during the Renaissance, most notably by Marsilio Ficino. It holds that a single, primordial wisdom was revealed by God to ancient sages like Hermes Trismegistus, Zoroaster, and Orpheus, which eventually flowed into the works of Plato.</p>
